<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2677" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴσιμος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, also
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Od.
			23.14
		</span></i>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἶσα</span>):—
			Ep.
		
		Adj.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>appointed by the will of the
				gods, destined</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴ.
			ἦμαρ</span> the <i>fatal</i> day of death, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				8.72
			</span></i>, Bacisap.<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				9.43
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴσιμόν ἐστι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					21.291
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>agreeable to the decree of fate, meet, fitting</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴσιμα εἰπεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					22.46
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴσιμα εἰδώς</span>, opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴσυλα ῥέζειν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				2.231
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρένας αἰσίμη</span>
			<i>right</i>-minded, <i><span class="en">
				23.14
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴσιμα πίνειν</span> to drink
				<i>in decent measure</i>, <i><span class="en">
				21.294
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
